[31m-Camera access on macOS belongs to the app that runs Python: run `make app` from **Terminal**[m
[31m-and allow camera access there (System Settings → Privacy & Security → Camera).[m
[32m+[m[32mBy contrast, **every laptop already has a standard 30 FPS RGB webcam**—but consumer webcams face fundamental physical constraints:[m
[32m+[m[32m1. **Low Spatial Resolution at the Eye**: At a normal reading distance of $50\text{–}70\text{ cm}$, a reader's entire iris spans only **12–18 pixels** in a $640 \times 480$ webcam frame.Moving your gaze vertically from one line of text to the next rotates your eyeball by **$< 0.8^\circ$**, shifting the iris center by **less than 1 pixel**.[m
[32m+[m[32m2. **Head-Pose Coupling**: A tiny $1^\circ$ head tilt or a $1\text{ cm}$ slouch shifts the eye appearance in the camera frame far more than a reading saccade across a sentence.[m
[32m+[m[32m3. **The Problem with Existing Webcam Gaze Demos**: Almost all webcam eye-tracking demos display a jittery red dot and falsely claim word-level precision, without ever measuring or accounting for the webcam's actual error radius ($\sim 2^\circ\text{–}3^\circ$, or **$35\text{–}75\text{ px}$** on screen).[m
