[32m+[m[32m## 🧠 Computer Vision & Mathematical Pipeline[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### 1. MediaPipe 478-Point 3D Mesh & 5-Point Iris Geometry[m
[32m+[m[32mImplemented in [`src/gazeread/features/landmarks.py`](src/gazeread/features/landmarks.py) and [`src/gazeread/gaze/backend_landmark.py`](src/gazeread/gaze/backend_landmark.py):[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- **478 3D Landmarks**: MediaPipe `FaceLandmarker` runs in temporal `VIDEO` mode (`output_facial_transformation_matrixes=True`), outputting 468 facial mesh vertices plus **10 dedicated iris landmarks** (`468..472` for the subject's right eye, `473..477` for the left eye).[m
[32m+[m[32m- **5-Point Iris Centroid (`iris_center_5pt`)**: Instead of relying on a single center landmark, GazeRead averages the pupil center with its 4 cardinal iris-ring vertices:[m
[32m+[m[32m  $$\mathbf{c}_{\text{iris}} = \frac{1}{5}\sum_{k \in \{\text{center}, \text{ring}_{1..4}\}} \mathbf{p}_k$$[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Eye-Coordinate Projection ($u, v$)**: For each eye (`right`: corners `33, 133`, lids `159, 145`; `left`: corners `263, 362`, lids `386, 374`), the iris offset is projected onto the local inner-to-outer corner axis $\hat{\mathbf{e}}_u$ and its image-downward perpendicular $\hat{\mathbf{e}}_v$, normalized by the eye corner width $w_{\text{eye}} = \|\mathbf{p}_{\text{outer}} - \mathbf{p}_{\text{inner}}\|$:[m
[32m+[m[32m  $$u = \frac{(\mathbf{c}_{\text{iris}} - \mathbf{c}_{\text{eye}}) \cdot \hat{\mathbf{e}}_u}{w_{\text{eye}}}, \qquad v = \frac{(\mathbf{c}_{\text{iris}} - \mathbf{c}_{\text{eye}}) \cdot \hat{\mathbf{e}}_v}{w_{\text{eye}}}$$[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Eyelid Openness & Blink Gate**:[m
[32m+[m[32m  $$\text{openness} = \frac{\|\mathbf{p}_{\text{upper}} - \mathbf{p}_{\text{lower}}\|}{w_{\text{eye}}}$$[m
[32m+[m[32m  Frames with $\text{openness} < 0.15$ on either eye are immediately flagged as `valid = False` (blinks), pausing calibration sample collection and holding the One-Euro filter state.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### 2. 6-DoF Head Pose Extraction[m
[32m+[m[32mImplemented in [`src/gazeread/features/head_pose.py`](src/gazeread/features/head_pose.py):[m
[32m+[m[32m- Extracts the $3\times 3$ rotation block $\mathbf{R}$ and 3D translation vector $\mathbf{t} = (t_x, t_y, t_z)$ in centimetres from MediaPipe's $4\times 4$ canonical face transformation matrix.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Computes ZYX Euler angles $(\text{yaw}, \text{pitch}, \text{roll})$ in degrees and gates out extreme head turns ($|\text{yaw}| > 30^\circ$ or $|\text{pitch}| > 25^\circ$).[m
[32m+[m[32m- Supplies the **12-D Biometric Feature Vector**:[m
[32m+[m[32m  $$\mathbf{x} = \big[u_R, v_R, u_L, v_L, \text{open}_R, \text{open}_L, \text{yaw}, \text{pitch}, \text{roll}, t_x, t_y, t_z\big]^\top$$[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### 3. Method B: Deep Appearance Gaze with L2CS-Net[m
[32m+[m[32mImplemented in [`src/gazeread/gaze/backend_l2cs.py`](src/gazeread/gaze/backend_l2cs.py) and [`src/gazeread/gaze/l2cs_model.py`](src/gazeread/gaze/l2cs_model.py):[m
[32m+[m[32m- Crops a $1.2\times$ square bounding box around the detected facial landmarks, resizes to $448\times 448$, and passes it through a **ResNet-50 L2CS-Net** backbone (official Gaze360 weights).[m
[32m+[m[32m- Decodes 90 discrete $4^\circ$ bins via softmax expectation for both gaze yaw and pitch, optionally combined with MediaPipe head pose (`B+pose`), allowing side-by-side paired comparisons (`--compare`) against Method A on the exact same calibration dots.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### 4. Closed-Form Leave-One-Out (LOO) Ridge Calibration[m
[32m+[m[32mImplemented in [`src/gazeread/gaze/calibration.py`](src/gazeread/gaze/calibration.py):[m
[32m+[m[32m- Standardizes features across the $N \in \{9, 16\}$ shuffled calibration dots and evaluates both **Affine (Degree 1)** and **Quadratic (Degree 2)** polynomial expansions across a 15-point logarithmic grid of Ridge penalties $\alpha \in [10^{-4}, 10^3]$ (leaving the intercept unpenalized).[m
[32m+[m[32m- Computes exact **Leave-One-Dot-Out (LOO) residuals** in closed form using the leverage entries $H_{ii}$ of the hat matrix $\mathbf{H} = \mathbf{A}(\mathbf{A}^\top\mathbf{A} + \mathbf{P}_\alpha)^{-1}\mathbf{A}^\top$:[m
[32m+[m[32m  $$\mathbf{r}_i^{\text{LOO}} = \frac{\mathbf{y}_i - \hat{\mathbf{y}}_i}{1 - H_{ii}}$$[m
[32m+[m[32m- Degree 2 is selected only if it beats Degree 1's LOO RMS error by at least $10\%$ (`poly2_margin = 0.10`), preventing overfitting on 9-point grids.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### 5. Adaptive One-Euro Filtering, I-DT Fixations & Soft Gaussian Mapping[m
[32m+[m[32mImplemented in [`src/gazeread/gaze/filters.py`](src/gazeread/gaze/filters.py), [`src/gazeread/analysis/fixations.py`](src/gazeread/analysis/fixations.py), and [`src/gazeread/analysis/line_mapping.py`](src/gazeread/analysis/line_mapping.py):[m
[32m+[m[32m- **2D One-Euro Filter**: Dynamically increases the low-pass cutoff frequency $f_c = f_{c,\min} + \beta |\dot{x}|$ during fast saccades (eliminating lag) while heavily smoothing slow fixation jitter.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Zero-Effort Page Micro-Drift Lock**: Pulses a $350\text{ ms}$ visual anchor on the first word of each new page, applying a bounded EWMA offset correction ($\le 55\text{ px}$) to cancel out slow postural slouching between pages.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Soft Gaussian Line & Paragraph Mapping**: Each fixation or gaze sample $(x, y, \Delta t)$ within the text column distributes its time $\Delta t$ across lines $i = 1\dots M$ with Gaussian weights scaled by the user's measured vertical validation error $\sigma_y$:[m
[32m+[m[32m  $$w_i(y) = \frac{\exp\!\left(-\frac{(y - y_{c,i})^2}{2\sigma_y^2}\right)}{\sum_{j=1}^M \exp\!\left(-\frac{(y - y_{c,j})^2}{2\sigma_y^2}\right)}$$[m
[32m+[m
