[32m+[m[32m## 📖 Plain-English Glossary of Every Technical Term[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mWe designed the UI so **normal users see clear, everyday English**, while researchers can still inspect the underlying mathematical metrics:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m| Technical Term in Code/Logs | Plain-English UI Label | What It Actually Means |[m
[32m+[m[32m| :--- | :--- | :--- |[m
[32m+[m[32m| **$\sigma_{\text{px}}$ (`sigma_px`)** | **Tracking Accuracy** | Your overall gaze error radius in screen pixels, measured on 5 test dots *after* calibration. Lower is better ($\sim 40\text{–}75\text{ px}$ is typical on a laptop webcam). |[m
[32m+[m[32m| **$\sigma_y$ (`rms_y`)** | **Vertical Error vs. Line Height** | How much your predicted gaze bounces up and down vertically. Because reading lines are stacked vertically, $\sigma_y$ determines whether the camera can tell lines apart. |[m
[32m+[m[32m| **`granularity` (`line` vs `paragraph`)** | **Webcam Tracking Clarity** | **Line-by-Line** if $\sigma_y \le \frac{1}{2}\text{Line Height}$ ($33\text{ px}$); otherwise **Paragraph Clarity** (so the app never lies about line accuracy when noise is too high). |[m
[32m+[m[32m| **`loo_rms_px` (LOO RMS)** | **Calibration Fit Quality** | Leave-One-Out cross-validation error during calibration: predicts each calibration dot from the *other* dots to verify you didn't blink or look away. |[m
[32m+[m[32m| **One-Euro Filter** | **Adaptive Gaze Smoothing** | A speed-aware filter that keeps the gaze spotlight rock-steady when you stare at a word, but snaps instantly when your eyes jump to a new line. |[m
[32m+[m[32m| **I-DT Fixation** | **Eye Pause / Fixation** | When your eyes lock onto a small region for $\ge 100\text{ ms}$. Reading is a sequence of fixations (where comprehension happens) separated by fast jumps (*saccades*). |[m
[32m+[m[32m| **Regression** | **Backtracking (Re-read)** | When your eyes jump *backward* to an earlier part of the same line or an earlier line in the paragraph because a sentence was dense or confusing. |[m
[32m+[m[32m| **Return Sweep** | **Line-to-Line Sweep** | The diagonal eye movement from the right end of one line to the left start of the next line down. |[m
[32m+[m[32m| **Soft Gaussian Mapping** | **Smooth Attention Glow** | Instead of assigning 100% of a noisy gaze point to whichever line is 1 pixel closer, it shares credit smoothly across nearby lines based on your camera's $\sigma_y$. |[m
[32m+[m
